---
/**
 * P5 Foundations and CSR: /partner-with-us/foundations/ (T3, implements doc 04 matrix 4.3).
 * C1 to C14 in order, as the numbered table in doc 06 P5, without C3 (Cost of Waiting) and C4 (Imagine), which the audience pages leave to Home since WP47.
 * WP30c (owner direction 2026-10-14, "less is more"): every CMF band stays, each states its point once. Gone: the In Short summary, the fit check, the evidence-and-fit brief,
 * the reporting-and-recognition paragraph (the features row carries it), the full review cycle (it lives on the partnership overview, as on the Development Partners page)
 * and the restated three-step mechanism. The two inquiry links now sit directly under the two-route comparison they belong to (cycle-7 IA review).
 * WP35 (cycle-12 review): the trial and the survey are shown once, as tiles in Results at a Glance; the proof band that restated them is a one-line strip of links (#proof-band). The WSDFM tile is gone
 * from the glance (its 71% is program records, read beside the trial's 63.1%; the Kosovo program result takes its place), the evaluator is spelled out where the page first names it, the independent-evidence
 * row says the evidence is on the predecessor program, and the meta description is a complete sentence.
 * WP36 (cycle-13 reviews): the +$27 tile reads "estimated monthly income gain for women offered a place in a predecessor program, versus a control mean of about $66" (RC-04's stat label); the three pains are
 * statements; the cost and safeguarding questions have the one-line route answers, each with a link to the full answer.
 * WP37 (cycle-14 review): the Funding Route 2 passage under the offer cards no longer retells the platform and its live and pre-launch list (the comparison above it has them); it says what a platform grant
 * supports in one sentence and links the platform-grant inquiry.
 * WP39 (cycle-16 review): "What Your Cohort Grant Gets" is three short cards (IncludesBand), not the funder concern / what is included / practical benefit matrix.
 * WP40 (cycle-17 review): the third pain is about accountability keeping pace with scale (it read as a swipe at other implementers); the two links under "Two Ways to Fund the Path" are "Explore YouthWIDE Delivery" and
 * "Explore JobReady’s Rollout", one for each route, in place of "See Funding Route 1 / 2" and the platform link beside them; "Reporting and Review" says what the reports and reviews do; the closing
 * "It doesn’t have to be this way." line of the cost band is gone.
 * WP43 (cycle-20 review): the problem band's heading is "Fund Training That Reaches Paid Work" (it was "Grants Buy Hours. You Want Earnings"); the first pain below it still says that grants buy hours, but rarely earnings.
 * WP46 (cycle-22 review): "What Happens After You Say Yes" has the four Development Partners steps, scoped "For cohort grants." (the call-to-action band above keeps what is discussed for a platform grant), and the cohort timing that the
 * call-to-action urgency line carried is now the steps' own; the closing partner line reads "Organizations that have worked with CodersTrust include the Rockefeller Foundation, DANIDA and Porticus." (it was "Development and NGO partners include ...", which mislabeled the foundations among them).
 * WP47 (owner decision 2026-10-15): the page opens with its own proof and goes straight to its offer. The Cost of Waiting band ("Every Year of Delay Leaves a Cohort Without a Route to Work") and the Imagine band ("What a Funded
 * Cohort Could Show") are gone; Home carries them. No gate or test needed them here: the page's problem band is statements without a tile (as before), so the 62 million (PX-01) that the cost band's first
 * card carried is now left to Home; the monthly reports and the follow-up surveys they mentioned are in the cards, the FAQ and "Reporting and Review". Funding Route 2's platform status reads "Live today: partner portals and AI chat."
 * (the subset Investors uses; JobReady Platform keeps the full list).
 * WP48 (cycle-23 review): the "Reporting and Review" callout before the call to action is gone; the "Progress You Can See Every Month" card already says the page's reporting (monthly reports, a quarterly steering review, the pilot scorecard).
 * WP49 (cycle-24 reviews): the "Progress You Can See Every Month" card is two sentences (monthly reports and quarterly reviews keep progress visible; where agreed, SDG-mapped reporting follows the CSR framework, with co-branded certificates and events):
 * the scorecard is stated by the first two cards, the Accountability callout (thresholds, cost per completer and per verified outcome) and the session agenda, and the contracting entity and due-diligence confirmation by the Due Diligence band, so the card
 * no longer repeats them; the first card says results are measured "against the agreed scorecard, including first paid work, not attendance alone" (the scorecard also covers completion, certification and sustained work, PD-11);
 * the "Choose Where to Start" lead no longer repeats the cost answer's pricing sentence (the "What Does It Cost?" answer states it); the fourth glance tile (the Kosovo result) is part of "Results at a Glance" (a single tile needs no
 * "More Results" heading); the steps band is "What Happens Next" (lead "For cohort grants."). The two route actions under "Two Ways to Fund the Path" are text links, as the brief asks (FundingRoutes).
 * WP50 (cycle-25 review): the first pain is "Track earnings, not only training hours" (Title Case when rendered; it said that grants "rarely" buy earnings, a statement about all grants), and the track-record band opens with its origin line
 * ("Since 2014, ..."): the empathy line that restated the problem ("You want your grant to change a young person’s income, ...") is gone, because the problem band above says it. "Discuss a JobReady Platform Grant" was linked twice (under the funding-routes
 * comparison and in the Funding Route 2 passage); the passage keeps its one sentence and the link stays beside the comparison (WP37 had added it to the passage). "Discuss a YouthWIDE Cohort Grant" was linked once, so it is unchanged.
 * WP51 (cycle-26 review): the closing partner line under "What Happens Next" ("Organizations that have worked with CodersTrust include the Rockefeller Foundation, DANIDA and Porticus.") moved, unchanged, into the Track Record
 * band ("We’ve Built This Path Since 2014"), directly after the BIGD line (C14.validateFor.foundations is passed to PartnerGuideBand's `statements`); the page now ends on its first-action line alone, as Development Partners and Governments do since WP50.
 * WP52 (cycle-27 review): the cohort-grant offer's lead is the program-sizes note alone; "Prefer to fund the platform? See JobReady Platform Grants below." is gone (the funding-route comparison above carries the platform-grant row and its inquiry link,
 * and the Funding Route 2 passage below keeps its #platform-grants id, which no link points to).
 * WP57 (cycle-29 review, Grok R6): the +$27 tile reads "about +$27" ("about" is the register's own word for it: RC-04 opens "About +$27 a month"), as Home and the trial page say it.
 * WP57 (cycle-29 review, Kimi K3, item K2): the meta description reads "... found women offered a place earned an estimated $27 more a month." (RC-04's "+$27 a month", still read from the register by factPart); it said "had an estimated $27 higher monthly income".
 * WP60 (cycle-32 review, Gemini GM4 and GM9): "What Happens Next" opens "For platform grants, the first conversation covers JobReady’s infrastructure and staged rollout. For cohort grants, the steps are below." before the four cohort steps (it covered cohort grants only);
 * Samina's learner card shows her outcome line alone ("Completed 90+ projects as a freelance graphic designer on Fiverr"): the sentence under it, "She has completed 90+ projects on Fiverr so far.", repeated it (flagged in three cycles) and is gone.
 * WP62 (cycle-34 review, Grok, GPT-6.1 Sol and Gemini): the randomized trial filled two of the four glance tiles (+10.3 percentage points and about +$27), so the fourth tile is the WSDFM program-record tile (PR-01: "711 of 1,000", "WSDFM program records: 71% in work",
 * tagged Program Record) in place of the +$27 tile. The +$27 is not stated elsewhere in the page body; the meta description still says it (RC-04, read by factPart).
 * WP62 rework (R3): the tile carries the note the Impact page's WSDFM tile has, WSDFM_NOT_TRIAL_NOTE ("Program records, separate from the randomized trial of the predecessor program, which studied 833 women."; src/data/copy.ts), since WP35 had taken the tile off this
 * page because its 71% read beside the trial's figures; the tile's data-fact names RC-07 (the 833) and PR-06 beside PR-01, as Impact's does.
 * WP65 (cycle-37 review, GPT-6.1 Sol, Gemini): "711 of 1,000" stood in Results at a Glance and again on the Proof in Practice WSDFM card, with the not-the-trial note twice. UNDP YES, Korail was on no other part of this page (the UNDP logo in the
 * partner strip is the organization's, not the program), so the glance's fourth tile is the UNDP YES, Korail program-record tile (PR-03: 67% of the 350 enrolled found their first job within three months, 2017; the label is Development Partners',
 * UNDP_YES_TILE_LABEL in partners.ts) in place of the WSDFM tile, and the WSDFM records with their "not trial data" caption are stated once, on the Proof in Practice card.
 * WP75 (owner answer 2026-10-22): the 350 is the number enrolled (PR-03 said "trained"), so the tile reads "of the 350 enrolled in UNDP YES, Korail (2017), found their first job within three months".
 * "Two Ways to Fund the Path": Route 2's evidence cell is "Youth-program outcomes are not platform outcomes." alone (FundingRoutes; Gemini).
 * WP66 (owner request 2026-10-20): the Track Record band's list closes with the signed-agreement sentence for development partners and NGOs (SC-11c, `signed` on PartnerGuideBand: "CodersTrust has signed MOUs, agreements or contracts with ... development partners and NGOs."),
 * after the BIGD line and the names line (which keeps its place directly after the BIGD line); the band's heading says "Since 2014", so the sentence leaves the year to it.
 */
import PartnerGlance from '../../../components/pages/partners/PartnerGlance.astro';
import PairedEvidence from '../../../components/pages/partners/PairedEvidence.astro';
import DueDiligenceView from '../../../components/pages/hub/DueDiligenceView.astro';
import LearnerVoice from '../../../components/pages/impact/LearnerVoice.astro';
import LandingLayout from '../../../layouts/LandingLayout.astro';
import HeroBand from '../../../components/sections/HeroBand.astro';
import DefinitionBand from '../../../components/sections/DefinitionBand.astro';
import ProblemBand from '../../../components/sections/ProblemBand.astro';
import MechanismBand from '../../../components/sections/MechanismBand.astro';
import CaseStudyCarousel from '../../../components/sections/CaseStudyCarousel.astro';
import IncludesBand from '../../../components/sections/IncludesBand.astro';
import FAQBand from '../../../components/sections/FAQBand.astro';
import NextStepsBand from '../../../components/sections/NextStepsBand.astro';
import CTABand from '../../../components/ui/CTABand.astro';
import SessionAgenda from '../../../components/ui/SessionAgenda.astro';
import GainsPains from '../../../components/pages/partners/GainsPains.astro';
import PartnerGuideBand from '../../../components/pages/partners/PartnerGuideBand.astro';
import SubBand from '../../../components/pages/partners/SubBand.astro';
import Callout from '../../../components/pages/partners/Callout.astro';
import OfferCards from '../../../components/pages/partners/OfferCards.astro';
import FundingRoutes from '../../../components/pages/partners/FundingRoutes.astro';
import Reinforcement from '../../../components/pages/partners/Reinforcement.astro';
import PageEnhancements from '../../../components/pages/partners/PageEnhancements.astro';
import { KOSOVO_WOW_TILE_LABEL, LINKS, TRACKING_MONTHS, UNDP_YES_TILE_LABEL, factPart, funderOptionCards, meta } from '../../../components/pages/partners/partners';
import { BIGD_NAME, C14, HEADLINE, POSITIONING, PROGRAM_SIZES_NOTE, VALUE_PROPOSITION, WB_KOSOVO } from '../../../data/copy';
import { faqJsonLd } from '../../../lib/faq';
import { cta } from '../../../lib/mailto';
import { webPage } from '../../../lib/schema';

const PATH = '/partner-with-us/foundations/';
const primary = cta('funding');
// WP27: the two funding routes each get a text link with its own prefilled subject, under the one primary button; WP30c: they sit under the two-route comparison.
const routeYouthwide = cta('fundingYouthwide');
const routePlatform = cta('fundingPlatform');
// The partner-edition report request (doc 04 §7), straight from the shared CTA library.
const reportCta = cta('report');
const report = { label: reportCta.label, href: reportCta.href };

const { title, description } = meta(
  'Fund Youth Employment: Foundations and CSR',
  `Fund a supported path to earnings. A randomized trial of a predecessor program found women offered a place earned an estimated ${factPart('RC-04', /\+(\$\d+) a month/)} more a month.`,
);

// Q8-route and Q9-route: the one-line cost and safeguarding answers, each with a link to where the full answer lives (the partner hub FAQ, the governance page) (WP36).
const FAQ_IDS = ['Q3', 'Q8-route', 'Q9-route', 'Q10'];
---

<LandingLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={PATH}
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Partner with Us', href: LINKS.hub }, { label: 'Foundations and CSR' }]}
  jsonLd={[webPage({ path: PATH, name: title, description }), faqJsonLd('foundations', PATH, FAQ_IDS)]}
  stickyCta={{ label: primary.label, href: primary.href }}
>
  <!-- C1 · Identity hook -->
  <HeroBand
    audience="For Foundations and CSR Leaders"
    title={HEADLINE.foundations}
    lead={VALUE_PROPOSITION.foundations}
    cta={{ label: primary.label, href: primary.href }}
    artSeed="partners-foundations"
  />
  <!-- GEO · What is CodersTrust? -->
  <DefinitionBand />
  <!-- WP58 (cycle-30 review, GLM L3): the +10.3 trial tile (RC-02, the strongest evidence) is the first tile; the survey and Kosovo tiles follow. WP62 (cycle-34 review): the fourth tile, the single `more` tile that joins the main group, was the WSDFM program-record tile (PR-01),
       where it had been the +$27 tile (RC-04): the trial filled two of the four tiles. WP65 (cycle-37 review): it is the UNDP YES, Korail program-record tile (PR-03, as Development Partners shows it), because WSDFM's "711 of 1,000" is on the Proof in Practice card below. -->
  <PartnerGlance
    lead={[{ id: 'RC-02', href: '/impact/independent-evaluation/' }, { id: 'OC-03', href: '/impact/outcomes-2026/' }, { id: 'PR-02', href: '/impact/case-studies/kosovo-women-in-online-work/', label: KOSOVO_WOW_TILE_LABEL, note: WB_KOSOVO.text, also: WB_KOSOVO.facts }]}
    more={[{ id: 'PR-03', href: LINKS.caseUndp, label: UNDP_YES_TILE_LABEL }]}
  />
  <LearnerVoice story="samina-tasneem-chowdhury" program="WSDFM" tone="white" />

  <!-- C2 · Problem -->
  <ProblemBand
    title="Fund Training That Reaches Paid Work"
    bluf="You want to know what your grant changed, not only how many hours it paid for."
    factIds={['PX-01']}
  >
    <GainsPains
      slot="lead"
      pains={[
        // WP91 (triage A10): a "Must" title, as the page's other "Must" card; the body sentence is unchanged.
        { q: 'Earnings must be tracked, not only training hours', text: 'Attendance is easy to count; a change in income is harder to show.' },
        // WP48 (cycle-23 review): "Independent evidence on youth-employment programs is thin." was a claim about the whole sector; the card states the funder's need instead.
        { q: 'Independent evidence is hard to find', text: 'You need independent evidence, not a provider’s own count.' },
        // WP38 (cycle-15 review): a general funder pain, stated in one line like its two neighbors; it rests on no CodersTrust fact. WP40 (cycle-17 review): worded as the funder's need, not as a comparison with other implementers.
        { q: 'Accountability must keep pace with scale', text: 'You need monthly outcome reports as delivery expands.' },
      ]}
    />
  </ProblemBand>

  <!-- C3 (Cost of Waiting) and C4 (Imagine) are left to Home since WP47 (owner decision 2026-10-15). -->

  <!-- C5 · Guide. WP50 (cycle-25 review): no empathy line; the band opens with the origin line, since the problem band above states the problem. -->
  <PartnerGuideBand
    statements={[
      { facts: ['PR-01', 'RC-01'], markers: ['RC-01'], text: `The ${BIGD_NAME} evaluated the predecessor WSDFM program, commissioned by Porticus, in a randomized trial.` },
      // WP51 (cycle-26 review, Kimi m1): the partner line that closed the page under "What Happens Next" moved here, unchanged, directly after the BIGD line.
      C14.validateFor.foundations,
    ]}
    signed="SC-11c"
    method={{ text: 'Our TalentLEAP method organizes skills into career paths.', link: { label: 'How TalentLEAP Works', href: LINKS.talentleap } }}
    partnerGroup="development"
    strip
  />

  <!-- C6 · Mechanism (two funding routes). WP25s: one chooser, one naming scheme: Funding Route 1 (YouthWIDE Cohort Grants) and Funding Route 2 (JobReady Platform Grants), in the same order here and in the two offer bands below.
       WP40 (cycle-17 review): the two links under the comparison are one for each route, named for what they open ("Explore YouthWIDE Delivery": the program page; "Explore JobReady’s Rollout": the platform page and its rollout status),
       in place of "See Funding Route 1 / 2" (jumps to the offer bands, #cohort-grants and #platform-grants, which keep their ids) and a separate "About the JobReady Platform" link to the same page as the second. -->
  <div class="pp-two">
    <MechanismBand
      title="Two Ways to Fund the Path"
      positioning={POSITIONING.foundations}
      diagram={false}
      moreLinks={[
        { label: 'Explore YouthWIDE Delivery', href: LINKS.youthwide },
        { label: 'Explore JobReady’s Rollout', href: LINKS.platform },
      ]}
    >
      <!-- WP29 (benchmark review): the two routes as a two-row comparison (What It Supports, Evidence Relationship), in place of the two route cards. Their sentences moved into it; nothing was added. -->
      <!-- WP30c (cycle-7 IA review): the two inquiry links sit directly under the comparison they belong to, not in the hero before the routes are explained. -->
      <FundingRoutes inquiries={[routeYouthwide, routePlatform]} />
    </MechanismBand>
  </div>

  <!-- C7 · Proof: the trial and survey results are the tiles above; this strip links the full evidence (WP35, cycle-12 review) -->
  <PairedEvidence
    id="proof-band"
    eyebrow="The Evidence"
    title="See the Evidence Behind the Results"
    lead="The trial evaluated a predecessor program; the survey describes what completers who responded report about work and income."
    items={[]}
    broader={[
      { label: 'Read the Trial Results', href: LINKS.trial },
      { label: 'Impact Survey 2026', href: LINKS.outcomes },
    ]}
    broaderLabel="The evidence behind the results"
  />
  <CaseStudyCarousel
    title="Proof in Practice"
    items={[
      { title: 'Women’s Skill Development for Freelancing Marketplace (WSDFM)', program: 'Commissioned by Porticus', factId: 'PR-01', href: LINKS.caseWsdfm },
      { title: 'Her Power', program: 'ICT Division / Department of ICT (DoICT)', factId: 'PR-05', href: LINKS.caseHerPower },
    ]}
  />

  <!-- C8 · Features to benefits. WP39 (cycle-16 review): three short cards in place of the concern / inclusion / benefit matrix, in the order of the three pains in C2 (grants buy hours, rarely earnings; independent evidence is
       hard to find; accountable implementers are hard to find). The fourth row (SDG-mapped reporting, co-branded certificates and events, "Added Benefit") joins the reporting card as its second sentence, so nothing it said is lost.
       Each sentence rests on the register: PD-01 and PD-02 (mentoring and placement support; outcome tracking for 12 months after each course, in the standard inclusions), PD-11 (the pilot scorecard; WP44: the second card is the scorecard, not the predecessor trial, because it describes a deliverable), PD-08 (monthly reports and the quarterly steering review) and PD-18 (SDG-mapped reporting, co-branded certificates and events).
       WP49 (cycle-24 review): the third card no longer lists the scorecard (the first two cards, the Accountability callout and the agenda state it) or the contracting entity and due-diligence documents (the Due Diligence band states them), so its facts are PD-08 and PD-18. -->
  <IncludesBand
    title="What Your Cohort Grant Gets"
    cards={[
      {
        icon: 'target',
        title: 'Mentoring, Placement Support and Outcome Tracking',
        text: `Mentoring and placement support are standard inclusions, and outcomes are tracked for ${TRACKING_MONTHS} months after each course, as agreed in the program scope. Results are measured against the agreed scorecard, including first paid work, not attendance alone.`,
        facts: ['PD-01', 'PD-02', 'PD-11'],
      },
      {
        icon: 'badge-check',
        title: 'A Pilot Scorecard Agreed with You',
        text: 'Cost per completer and per verified outcome, with thresholds agreed before the first cohort starts.',
        facts: ['PD-11'],
      },
      {
        icon: 'file-check',
        title: 'Progress You Can See Every Month',
        text: 'Monthly reports and quarterly reviews keep progress visible. Where agreed, SDG-mapped reporting follows your CSR framework, with co-branded certificates and events.',
        facts: ['PD-08', 'PD-18'],
      },
    ]}
  />

  <!-- C9 · Objections -->
  <FAQBand
    audience="foundations"
    ids={FAQ_IDS}
    title="Questions About Cohort Grants"
  />

  <!-- C10 · Differentiation: the positioning statement opens C6; the comparison table is on Home and Investors only (WP30c). -->

  <!-- C11 · Offer -->
  <OfferCards
    id="cohort-grants"
    eyebrow="Funding Route 1 · YouthWIDE Cohort Grants"
    title="Choose Where to Start Your Cohort Grant"
    lead={PROGRAM_SIZES_NOTE}
    cards={funderOptionCards()}
    recommended={0}
  />
  <SubBand tone="airy" pull id="platform-grants">
    <Callout eyebrow="Funding Route 2 · JobReady Platform Grants">
      <!-- WP91 (triage A4): the sentence before the register line says the program sizes above are for cohort grants only, so the platform grant reads as the other route. -->
      <p data-fact="IN-04">The program sizes above apply to cohort grants only. A platform grant supports JobReady’s infrastructure and staged rollout, not cohorts.</p>
    </Callout>
  </SubBand>

  <!-- C12 · Risk reversal (immediately before C13): WP34 (cycle-11 review): the four diligence cards repeated what this page's bands state, so one item and a link stand in. WP45 (cycle-21 review) left a "Reporting and Review" callout
       after it; WP48 (cycle-23 review): that callout is gone, because its sentence (monthly reports track progress; quarterly reviews guide corrective action and any expansion) repeated the "Progress You Can See Every Month"
       card above (monthly reports and a quarterly steering review). The due-diligence item links to Governance and Accountability. -->
  <DueDiligenceView brief id="due-diligence" />

  <!-- C13 · Call to action -->
  <CTABand
    id="cta"
    heading="Let’s Explore a Funding Partnership"
    cta={{ label: primary.label, href: primary.href }}
    secondary={report}
  >
    <!-- WP34 (cycle-11 review): the funders here choose a cohort grant or a platform grant, so the line says what is discussed for each (the cohort-only discovery-session agenda is on the pages that sell cohorts). It is said once; the band below does not repeat it. -->
    <SessionAgenda lead="foundations" />
  </CTABand>

  <!-- C14 · Next steps -->
  <!-- WP46 (cycle-22 review): the band has the same four steps as Development Partners, scoped "For cohort grants." (a platform grant is scoped in the discovery session, which the C13 agenda above says). WP32 (cycle-9 review) had left the band
       without steps and kept the cohort timing in the C13 urgency line; the steps now carry that timing (about three weeks to agreement, 6–8 weeks from signing to training), so the urgency line that repeated it is gone, as on Development Partners.
       The "introductory call" sentence is gone with the stepless band: the page names one first step, the discovery session. -->
  <NextStepsBand lead="For platform grants, the first conversation covers JobReady’s infrastructure and staged rollout. For cohort grants, the steps below show target timing for grant-funded pilots." timing={false} />
  <Reinforcement logos={false} reminder={false} />

  <PageEnhancements />
</LandingLayout>
